# KNITRO options for the Melitz finite-delta bound outer NLP (Section 3, 2026-07-23
# governing-correction session). Minimal (partial) options file -- unlisted options keep
# KNITRO's own defaults. Modeled on ek_outer_loop_options.opt (algorithm=0, eval_fcga=no,
# quasi-Newton Hessian since no exact Hessian callback is supplied here) but with looser
# opttol than the Ricardian model's own tight settings: the divergence-budget constraint's
# gradient here comes from a finite-bandwidth secant or hand-derived branch derivative
# (Section 1), not an exact analytic Jacobian, so an opttol tighter than that gradient's
# own accuracy would either never satisfy KNITRO's stopping test or falsely report
# convergence on gradient noise.
algorithm       4
eval_fcga       no
gradopt         exact
hessopt         2
feastol         1e-7
feastol_abs     1e-8
opttol          1e-3
opttol_abs      1e-4
outlev          3
honorbnds       always
delta           0.05
maxit           2000
maxtime_real    240.0
